## 2. iMessage: the reconcile mechanism

### 2.1 New module `packages/imessage/src/lines.ts`

`remote/stream.ts:23` already imports from `../auth`, so `auth.ts` must not import `remote/stream.ts`. A third module both can import, keyed by array identity, consistent with the existing WeakMap idiom (`cloudAuthState` auth.ts:20, `pollCaches` cache.ts:86, `gates` profile-sync-gate.ts:91).

```ts
// packages/imessage/src/lines.ts — imports ./types ONLY. No cycle.
import type { RemoteClient } from "./types";

export interface LineObserver {
  attach(entry: RemoteClient): void;
  detach(entry: RemoteClient): Promise<void> | void;
}

export const setLineId:        (entry: RemoteClient, instanceId: string) => void;
export const getLineId:        (entry: RemoteClient) => string | undefined;
export const lineKey:          (entry: RemoteClient) => string;  // getLineId ?? stable WeakMap fallback
export const addLineObserver:  (clients: RemoteClient[], o: LineObserver) => void;
export const clearLineObservers: (clients: RemoteClient[]) => void;
export const notifyLineAttached: (clients: RemoteClient[], entry: RemoteClient) => void;
export const notifyLineDetached: (clients: RemoteClient[], entry: RemoteClient) => Promise<void>[];
```

- Backed by `WeakMap<RemoteClient[], Set<LineObserver>>` and `WeakMap<RemoteClient, string>`.
- `lineKey` falls back to a WeakMap-generated `line-${n}` for explicitly-configured clients (types.ts:19-27 permits two entries with the same `phone`, which would otherwise collide as group keys).
- **`notifyLineAttached` wraps each observer in try/catch and logs** — a throwing observer must never be able to break token renewal (see §2.3).

Import graph: `lines.ts → types.ts`; `auth.ts → lines.ts`; `remote/stream.ts → ../lines, ../auth`. Acyclic.

### 2.2 `auth.ts` rewrite

Delete `requirePhone` (auth.ts:22-28) and `syncPhones` (auth.ts:42-46) entirely; replace `records: {entry, instanceId}[]` with `Map<string, RemoteClient>`; hoist entry construction so startup and renewal share one code path.

```ts
const log = createLogger("spectrum.imessage.auth");  // same namespace createTokenRenewal({name:"imessage"}) already uses

const entries: RemoteClient[] = [];              // THE array; mutated in place forever
const records = new Map<string, RemoteClient>(); // instanceId -> entry

const buildEntry = (instanceId: string, phone: string, initialToken: string): RemoteClient => ({
  phone,
  client: createGrpcClient({
    address: `${instanceId}.imsg.photon.codes:443`,
    autoIdempotency: true,
    retry: true,
    tls: true,
    token: async () => {
      await renewal.refreshIfNeeded();
      const data = tokenData as DedicatedTokenData;
      return data.auth[instanceId] ?? initialToken;
    },
  }),
});
```

Byte-identical option set to auth.ts:104-117 — that is what §5.B asserts.

```ts
const reconcile = (data: DedicatedTokenData): void => {
  const next = Object.keys(data.auth ?? {});
  if (next.length === 0) {
    // Degenerate payload: never wipe a working set on a bad response.
    // (At startup `records` is empty, so this still yields [] — today's behavior.)
    log.warn("imessage token response contained no lines; keeping the current set");
    return;
  }

  for (const [instanceId, entry] of records) {          // removals
    if (data.auth[instanceId]) continue;
    records.delete(instanceId);
    const index = entries.indexOf(entry);
    if (index >= 0) entries.splice(index, 1);           // in place
    retire(instanceId, entry).catch((error) =>
      log.warn("failed to retire imessage line", { "spectrum.imessage.instance": instanceId, ...errorAttrs(error) }, error));
  }

  for (const instanceId of next) {                      // phone sync + additions
    const phone = data.numbers?.[instanceId];
    const existing = records.get(instanceId);
    if (existing) {
      if (phone) existing.phone = phone;
      else log.warn("imessage line lost its phone number; keeping the last known number",
                    { "spectrum.imessage.instance": instanceId });
      continue;
    }
    if (!phone) {                                       // FIXES latent bug #1
      log.warn("skipping imessage line without a phone number",
               { "spectrum.imessage.instance": instanceId });
      continue;
    }
    const entry = buildEntry(instanceId, phone, data.auth[instanceId] as string);
    setLineId(entry, instanceId);
    records.set(instanceId, entry);
    entries.push(entry);                                // in place
    notifyLineAttached(entries, entry);                 // SYNCHRONOUS, immediately after push
  }
};

// Detach the stream FIRST, then close the channel — closing a channel out from
// under a live resumableOrderedStream produces a reconnect-warn storm until the
// detach lands. Never awaited by refresh(): a wedged channel must not stall renewal.
const retire = async (instanceId: string, entry: RemoteClient): Promise<void> => {
  await Promise.allSettled(notifyLineDetached(entries, entry));
  await entry.client.close();
};
```

Then:

```ts
refresh: async () => {
  tokenData = await cloud.issueImessageTokens(projectId, projectSecret);
  lastRefreshAt = Date.now();
  if (tokenData.type !== "dedicated") return;
  try {
    reconcile(tokenData);
  } catch (error) {
    // Belt-and-braces: a reconcile throw would leave tokenExpiresAt unadvanced,
    // re-entering coalescedRefresh on EVERY subsequent RPC on EVERY line.
    log.error("imessage line reconcile failed", errorAttrs(error), error);
  }
},
```

Startup becomes `reconcile(dedicated)` against an empty `records`, then `cloudAuthState.set(entries, cloudAuth); return entries;`.

**Both latent bugs die here:**
- **#1** — a null/missing number is skipped-with-warning at startup (no more bricked boot) and at renewal (no more rejected `refresh()` → no more `refreshIfNeeded()` hammer-loop on every RPC on every line).
- **#2** — a deprovisioned instanceId is a *removal*, not a throw.

**Ordering guarantee:** push and `notifyLineAttached` are adjacent synchronous statements with no `await` between them, so `messages()` can never observe a half-applied array.

Add `clearLineObservers(clients)` to `disposeCloudAuth` (auth.ts:127-133).

**Shared mode is a structural no-op**: `reconcile` is behind `tokenData.type === "dedicated"`, `records` stays empty, no observer is ever notified. No branch needed.

### 2.3 `remote/stream.ts`: `messages()`

Replace `mergeStreams` (stream.ts:512-527) with the group; everything else in the function is unchanged.

```ts
export const messages = (clients, projectConfig?, profileSyncGate?): ManagedStream<IMessageMessage> => {
  const pollCache = getPollCache(clients);          // still keyed by the array — never replaced
  const staticShareEnabled = projectConfig?.profile?.imessageSynced === true;
  const recover = getCloudRecover(clients);
  // Frozen deliberately: only a shared array can make this false, and shared
  // arrays never reconcile.
  const includeGroupEvents = !isSharedMode(clients);

  const group = createStreamGroup<IMessageMessage>({ label: "imessage.messages" });
  const build = (entry: RemoteClient) => () => { /* exactly today's clientStream(...) call */ };

  for (const entry of clients) group.add(lineKey(entry), build(entry));

  if (!isSharedMode(clients)) {
    addLineObserver(clients, {
      attach: (entry) => { group.add(lineKey(entry), build(entry)); },
      detach: (entry) => group.remove(lineKey(entry)),
    });
  }
  return group;
};
```

Handling each case you listed:

| Case | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `messages()` **after** reconciles | The initial loop reads the live array, which is the truth. Nothing special. |
| `messages()` **before** reconciles | The observer fires `group.add` later; the group accepts pre-start *and* post-start adds. |
| `messages()` **never called** (webhook) | Observer set empty; `notifyLineAttached` iterates nothing. Array still mutates, so outbound sees new lines. Zero cost. |
| **shared mode** | `isSharedMode` short-circuits observer registration; `reconcile` never runs anyway. Double-guarded. |
| **null/missing phone** | Skipped with a warn in `reconcile`; never reaches the stream layer. |
| **empty `auth`** | Guarded in `reconcile`; the group is untouched. |
| **stream closed, then a reconcile fires** | `group.add`/`group.remove` return `false` on a closed group — the stale observer is inert. |
| **shutdown ordering** | spectrum.ts:857-895 closes streams (Phase 1) then `destroyClient` (Phase 3). Group close → `disposeCloudAuth` → `clearLineObservers`. A reconcile landing between the two is inert per the row above. |

